00:04:33.962 --> 00:04:39.042
with the Connected Machine agent network
requirements, give Microsoft Entra

67
00:04:39.042 --> 00:04:44.044
Government and Azure Government, with US
Gov regions and the dot us endpoints.

68
00:04:44.044 --> 00:04:46.007
The kit guards this both ways.

69
00:04:46.007 --> 00:04:50.190
The wave plan stops a server whose
region belongs to the other cloud,

70
00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:54.970
and the playbook that uses Microsoft's
role refuses any cloud but AzureCloud.

71
00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:58.810
For Azure Government, the kit's
other onboarding playbook,

72
00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:00.930
oh two, spells the steps out.

73
00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:09.215
Microsoft Learn's page, Connect machines
to Azure Arc at scale with Ansible,

74
00:05:09.215 --> 00:05:11.922
documents onboarding through the Azure Arc

75
00:05:11.922 --> 00:05:14.555
onboarding role in the
azure az collection.

76
00:05:14.555 --> 00:05:18.643
It installs the Connected Machine
agent and registers each host.

77
00:05:18.643 --> 00:05:22.973
The repository keeps a pinned copy
of the role's code, from the ansible

78
00:05:22.973 --> 00:05:27.304
collections azure repository at the
four point two point oh release.

79
00:05:27.304 --> 00:05:31.280
Running it offline, and reading its
code, shows what it leaves to you.

80
00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:34.362
It connects whatever
hosts the inventory names;

81
00:05:34.362 --> 00:05:37.830
the kit reads both owners and
